       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for a dose five times the maximum. A single 50 mg dose of amlodipine could cause profound, prolonged hypotension and shock in a 70 kg adult with normal organ function. Because the drug has a half-life of 30\u201350 hours, the effects would last for days. Giving it daily would make that worse.\n\nI can do any of the following:\n- Enter amlodipine **5 mg** or **10 mg** by mouth once daily right now.\n- Enter a different regimen if you want faster blood pressure control. Tell me the drug and dose, and I can enter it.\n- Leave the order for you to place directly with pharmacy review. If you have a clinical reason for the dose, pharmacy can help verify it and set up monitoring.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter it right away."
